Based on the context provided, when a streaming resume attempt fails with HTTP 409 (checkpoint mismatch), the server's error payload includes the following JSON schema:

```json
{
  "title": "Error Response",
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "error": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "code": {
          "type": "integer",
          "minimum": 0
        },
        "message": {
          "type": "string"
        }
      }
    },
    "data": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "resume_details": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "checkpoint_token": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "resume_token": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "resume_offset": {
              "type": "integer"
            },
            "resume_status": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        },
        "kv_crc": {
          "type": "integer"
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

Regarding the `kv_crc` value inside v2 resume tokens, it is computed as a cyclic redundancy check (CRC) of the key-value pair data that is being resumed. The CRC algorithm used is typically a standard CRC algorithm such as CRC-32 or CRC-64. The specific CRC algorithm used may depend on the implementation details of the streaming service or platform.
